{
  "about": [
    "Every place zm_qol creates a HUD element, which of the engine's two groups it lands in, and how long it lives.",
    "The engine sends a client at most 31 archived (.archived = 1, the default) and 31 non-archived (.archived = 0)",
    "hudelems per snapshot and silently drops the rest (HudElem_UpdateClient, 2013 PC server PDB; same 0x1F caps in",
    "the live r5346 t6zm image). Measured 2026-09-25 at a fresh TranZit spawn: archived 30/31, non-archived 8/31, which",
    "is why stock's buildable bar drew only its fill and subtitles came and went. See the HUD SLOT BUDGET banner in",
    "scripts/zm/qol_options.gsc. tools/check-hud-budget.ps1 enforces this table on every build.",
    "group: archived | current | server (a server element counts against EVERY client, in the archived group).",
    "life: permanent (held all match while its option is on) | ondemand (held while its thing exists, can overlap the",
    "permanent set) | transient (a user-invoked panel or a short pop-up) | dev (developer only) | alias (same element as",
    "another row, not counted twice)."
  ],
  "cap": 31,
